\chapter{Option, Result, and propagation}
\label{ch:30}
\index{Option, Result, and propagation}
\index{Cleanup!Result propagation}

The pervasive environment supplies canonical \OnxCodeTerm{Option<T>} and \OnxCodeTerm{Result<T,E>} declarations and copy-safe helper functions. Use Option for optional presence and Result for success with a typed error. On the admitted nominal Result, postfix \OnxCodeTerm{?} evaluates once, yields the success payload, or returns the active error to a compatible enclosing function after cleanup. For local recovery, use a match with both cases.

\OnxInputCode[firstline=3,lastline=15]{../../on1x/examples/pervasive_options.on1x}
The error code for a negative input differs from the error code for an odd input. Call the example with a positive even number and both kinds of invalid number to confirm the paths. The finite unique-owner profile makes \OnxCodeTerm{?} an explicit consuming site on a move-only result. Generic convenience helpers stay copy-safe and have different admissibility from an explicit owner-bearing construction and consumption. Option does not acquire Result propagation semantics simply because it also has two constructors.

